# The graveyard permission is only "using its warp ability": a card in the graveyard has no other way to be cast. Bot1 is at 1 life, so it
# cannot pay the warp cost's 2 life (CR 119.4), and with {B}{B} to spare the Culler in the graveyard is still not offered at its
# mana cost (`! Bot1.Graveyard.Timeline Culler.Cast` refuses every way). The positive control is
# timeline-culler-warped-from-the-graveyard-after-dying-then-exiled-and-recast-from-exile, the same position at 20 life.

